/-!
# The characterizations of a split node

Let `k` be a field, `X` a one-dimensional scheme locally of finite type over `k` and `x ∈ X` a
closed point. Three conditions on `x` agree: that `x` be a split node; that `x` be a node with
exactly two points of the normalization `X^ν` above it, both with residue field `k`; and that
the completed local ring `𝒪^∧_{X,x}` be the split-node power-series algebra `k[[x, y]]/(x y)`
over `k`.

This is Stacks Tag 0CBW. Condition (4) of the source is the placeholder "add more here" and
carries no mathematical content, so the equivalence proved is that of conditions (1), (2) and
(3).

## Main results

* `Stacks.Curves.isSplitNode_tfae_normalizationFibre_adicCompletion` — **the tag**: conditions
  (1), (2) and (3) are equivalent.
* `Stacks.Curves.nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X_of_isSplitNode` — condition
  (1) implies condition (3).
* `Stacks.Curves.isSplitNode_of_nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X` — condition
  (3) implies condition (1), with no nodality assumed.
* `Stacks.Curves.isSplitNode_iff_nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X` — those two
  conditions are equivalent.
* `Stacks.Curves.isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isSplitNode` — the local ring at a split node is a
  nodal `k`-algebra, the residue field being `k` and hence separable over it.
* `Stacks.Curves.isSeparableExtension_of_bijective_algebraMap` — a field extension with
  bijective structure map is separable.

## Implementation notes

The completed local ring is Mathlib's `AdicCompletion` at the maximal ideal of the stalk, and
the `k`-algebra structure on the stalk is the one induced by the germ at `x` of the structure
morphism, as everywhere in the node files. The split-node algebra is the quotient of
`MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k` by the ideal generated by the product of the two variables.

All three conditions run through the branch count. Splitness of the quadratic algebra of Tag
0CBT is two branches, by
`Stacks.Curves.nonempty_quadraticAlgebra_algEquiv_prod_iff_numberOfBranches_eq_two`; two
branches is the split-node presentation of the completion over the *residue field*
(`Stacks.Curves.nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X_iff_numberOfBranches_eq_two`),
and the residue field is `k` at a split node, so that presentation may be read with
coefficients in `k` after transporting along the coefficient isomorphism; and two branches is
two points of the fibre of the normalization
(`AlgebraicGeometry.numberOfBranches_eq_encard_normalizationFiber`, Tag 0C1S), which is the
count in condition (2).

The two points of condition (2) are named rather than counted, and the fibre is asserted to be
exactly the pair, which is the source's "there are exactly two points". That their residue
fields are `k` is `Stacks.Curves.bijective_fieldToResidue_normalization_of_isNodalAlgebra`, and
the converse passage from `κ(x₁) = k` back to `κ(x) = k` is
`Stacks.Curves.bijective_fieldToResidue_of_bijective_fieldToResidue_normalization`; both live
in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Curves/SplitNodeNormalizationFibre.lean`, which reads them
off the identification of the normalization fibre with the quadratic algebra of Tag 0CBT.

Condition (3) returns condition (1) with no nodality assumed. The presentation of the
completion forces `κ(x) = k`, because the residue field of a local quotient of a power-series
ring over `k` is `k` — a power series has the same residue as its constant term, and the
residue field of a local ring is that of its completion — and hence makes `κ(x)/k` separable;
the presentation also exhibits the completion as a nodal one with the isotropic coefficient
triple `(0, 1, 0)`, since `nodalBinaryQuadratic 0 1 0` is `x y`. Those two together are
condition (3) of `Stacks.Curves.isNodalAlgebra_tfae` (Tag 0C49), whose condition (1) is that
`𝒪_{X,x}` be a nodal `k`-algebra; nodality of `x` is then condition (2) ⟹ condition (1) of the
six equivalent conditions of Tag 0C4D, `Stacks.Curves.isNode_tfae_of_isClosed`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CBW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CBW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CBV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CBV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CBU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CBU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CBT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CBT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C4D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C4D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C49](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C49)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1S)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing
open Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u v

namespace Stacks.Curves

/-- A field extension whose structure map is bijective is separable. -/
public theorem isSeparableExtension_of_bijective_algebraMap (k : Type u) (K : Type v) [Field k]
    [Field K] [Algebra k K] (h : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k K)) :
    Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k K := by
  have e : k ≃ₐ[k] K := AlgEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.ofId k K) h
  refine ((Algebra.isSeparableExtension_tfae k K (ringExpChar k)).out 3 1).mp ?_
  have f : K ⊗[k] AdjoinPthRoots k ≃ₐ[k] AdjoinPthRoots k :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.congr e.symm AlgEquiv.refl).trans
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.lid k (AdjoinPthRoots k))
  exact isReduced_of_injective f.toRingHom f.injective

/-- A node whose residue field is the base field has a nodal local ring. -/
private theorem isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isNode_of_bijective (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 1) (x : X) (hnode : IsNode k X x)
    (hbij : Function.Bijective (fieldToResidue (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) x).hom) :
    letI : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
        X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    IsNodalAlgebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  let instK : Algebra k (X.residueField x) :=
    ((X.residue x).hom.comp ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫
      (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫ X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom).toAlgebra
  exact isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isNode_of_isSeparableExtension k X hdim x
    (isSeparableExtension_of_bijective_algebraMap k (X.residueField x) hbij) hnode

/-- The local ring at a split node is a nodal algebra over the base field. -/
public theorem isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isSplitNode (k : Type u) [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u})
    [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 1) (x : X) (hx : IsSplitNode k X x) :
    letI : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
        X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    IsNodalAlgebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
  isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isNode_of_bijective k X hdim x hx.1 hx.2.1

/-- Transport of the split-node power-series quotient along an isomorphism of coefficient
fields. -/
private noncomputable def splitNodeQuotientAlgEquiv {k K L : Type*} [Field k] [Field K]
    [Field L] [Algebra k K] [Algebra k L] (e : K ≃ₐ[k] L) :
    (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) K ⧸
        Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) K) * MvPowerSeries.X 1}) ≃ₐ[k]
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) L ⧸
        Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) L) * MvPowerSeries.X 1}) := by
  let E := mvPowerSeriesMapAlgEquiv e
  have hE : E ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) K) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) =
      (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) L) * MvPowerSeries.X 1 := by
    change MvPowerSeries.map (σ := Fin 2) e.toRingHom
      ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) K) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) = _
    simp
  have hI : Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) L) * MvPowerSeries.X 1} =
      (Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) K) *
        MvPowerSeries.X 1}).map E.toRingEquiv.toRingHom := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, ← hE]
    rfl
  exact Ideal.quotientEquivAlg _ _ E hI

/-- **The completed local ring at a split node of a one-dimensional curve is the split-node
power-series algebra over the base field.**

This is the implication (1) ⟹ (3) of Stacks Tag 0CBW; the tag itself is
`Stacks.Curves.isSplitNode_tfae_normalizationFibre_adicCompletion`. -/
public theorem nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X_of_isSplitNode
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 1) (x : X) (hx : IsSplitNode k X x) :
    letI : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
        X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    Nonempty (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) (X.presheaf.stalk x) ≃ₐ[k]
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸
        Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1})) := by
  let hLN : IsLocallyNoetherian X :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (X ↘ Spec (.of k))
  let instA : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
      X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
  let instK : Algebra k (X.residueField x) :=
    ((X.residue x).hom.comp ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫
      (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫ X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom).toAlgebra
  have hA : IsNodalAlgebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isSplitNode k X hdim x hx
  have hbr : numberOfBranchesOfLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) = 2 :=
    (nonempty_quadraticAlgebra_algEquiv_prod_iff_numberOfBranches_eq_two k
      (X.presheaf.stalk x) hA).mp hx.2.2
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := (nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X_iff_numberOfBranches_eq_two k
    (X.presheaf.stalk x) hA).mpr hbr
  have hbij : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (X.residueField x)) := hx.2.1
  exact ⟨e.trans (splitNodeQuotientAlgEquiv
    (AlgEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.ofId k (X.residueField x)) hbij).symm)⟩

/-- Bijectivity of `g` and of `f ∘ g` agree when `f` is bijective. -/
private theorem bijective_iff_of_bijective_comp_eq {α β γ : Type*} {f : β → γ} {g : α → β}
    {h : α → γ} (hf : Function.Bijective f) (hfg : ∀ a, f (g a) = h a) :
    Function.Bijective g ↔ Function.Bijective h := by
  obtain rfl : h = f ∘ g := funext fun a ↦ (hfg a).symm
  exact (hf.of_comp_iff' g).symm

/-- The product of the two variables lies in the maximal ideal of the two-variable
power-series ring. -/
private theorem X_mul_X_mem_maximalIdeal (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1 ∈
      maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
  Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (by
    rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff, MvPowerSeries.isUnit_iff_constantCoeff]
    simp)

/-- The residue field of a local quotient of a power-series ring over a field is the field: a
power series has the same residue as its constant term. -/
private theorem bijective_algebraMap_residueField_mvPowerSeries_quotient (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {σ : Type*} (I : Ideal (MvPowerSeries σ k)) [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries σ k ⧸ I)] :
    Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (ResidueField (MvPowerSeries σ k ⧸ I))) := by
  let P := MvPowerSeries σ k
  let Q := P ⧸ I
  let _ : IsLocalHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I : P →+* Q) :=
    IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  refine ⟨RingHom.injective _, fun z ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨qz, rfl⟩ := IsLocalRing.residue_surjective (R := Q) z
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective qz
  refine ⟨MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff p, ?_⟩
  calc
    algebraMap k (ResidueField Q) (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff p) =
        IsLocalRing.residue Q (Ideal.Quotient.mk I
          (MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff p))) := by
      rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k Q (ResidueField Q),
        IsLocalRing.ResidueField.algebraMap_eq, ← Ideal.Quotient.mk_algebraMap (R₁ := k) I,
        MvPowerSeries.algebraMap_apply]
      simp
    _ = IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I : P →+* Q)
        (IsLocalRing.residue P (MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff p))) := by
      rw [IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map_residue]
    _ = IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I : P →+* Q)
        (IsLocalRing.residue P p) := by
      rw [← residue_eq_residue_C_constantCoeff]
    _ = IsLocalRing.residue Q (Ideal.Quotient.mk I p) := by
      rw [IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map_residue]
    _ = IsLocalRing.residue Q qz := by rw [hp]

/-- **Stacks 0CBW, (3) ⟹ (1).** A closed point whose completed local ring is the split-node
power-series algebra over the base field is a split node.

Nodality is not assumed: the presentation of the completion exhibits the local ring as having a
nodal completion with coefficient triple `(0, 1, 0)`, which with the separability of `κ(x)/k`
makes it a nodal `k`-algebra by Stacks Tag 0C49, and clause (2) of the equivalences of Stacks
Tag 0C4D then returns the node. -/
public theorem isSplitNode_of_nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 1) (x : X) (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X))
    (hC :
      letI : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
        ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
          X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
      Nonempty (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) (X.presheaf.stalk x) ≃ₐ[k]
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸
          Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1}))) :
    IsSplitNode k X x := by
  let hLN : IsLocallyNoetherian X :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (X ↘ Spec (.of k))
  let instA : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
      X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
  let instK : Algebra k (X.residueField x) :=
    ((X.residue x).hom.comp ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫
      (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫ X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom).toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨eC⟩ := hC
  let A := X.presheaf.stalk x
  let C := AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A
  let P := MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k
  let I : Ideal P := Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : P) * MvPowerSeries.X 1}
  have hIle : I ≤ maximalIdeal P :=
    Ideal.span_le.mpr (by simpa using X_mul_X_mem_maximalIdeal k)
  let hnt : Nontrivial (P ⧸ I) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr
    (ne_top_of_le_ne_top (maximalIdeal.isMaximal P).ne_top hIle)
  let hloc : IsLocalRing (P ⧸ I) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hQ : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (ResidueField (P ⧸ I))) :=
    bijective_algebraMap_residueField_mvPowerSeries_quotient k I
  let φ : ResidueField C ≃ₐ[k] ResidueField (P ⧸ I) := IsLocalRing.ResidueField.mapAlgEquiv eC
  have hCres : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (ResidueField C)) :=
    (bijective_iff_of_bijective_comp_eq φ.bijective φ.commutes).mpr hQ
  have hρ : Function.Bijective (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap A C)) :=
    AdicCompletion.residueField_map_bijective A
  have hcompmap : ∀ a : k, IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap A C)
      (algebraMap k (X.residueField x) a) = algebraMap k (ResidueField C) a := by
    intro a
    calc
      IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap A C) (algebraMap k (X.residueField x) a) =
          IsLocalRing.residue C (algebraMap A C (algebraMap k A a)) := by
        rw [show algebraMap k (X.residueField x) a = IsLocalRing.residue A (algebraMap k A a) from
          rfl, IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map_residue]
      _ = algebraMap k (ResidueField C) a := by
        rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k C (ResidueField C),
          IsLocalRing.ResidueField.algebraMap_eq, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k A C]
  have hbij : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (X.residueField x)) :=
    (bijective_iff_of_bijective_comp_eq hρ hcompmap).mpr hCres
  -- the presentation of the completion, read with coefficients in the residue field
  let eK : AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A ≃ₐ[k]
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) (ResidueField A) ⧸
        Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) (ResidueField A)) *
          MvPowerSeries.X 1}) :=
    eC.trans (splitNodeQuotientAlgEquiv
      (AlgEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.ofId k (X.residueField x)) hbij))
  have hsep : Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k (ResidueField A) :=
    isSeparableExtension_of_bijective_algebraMap k (X.residueField x) hbij
  -- the presentation is a nodal completion, with the isotropic triple `(0, 1, 0)`
  have hNC : HasNodalCompletion k A := by
    refine ⟨0, 1, 0, by norm_num, ?_⟩
    rw [show nodalBinaryQuadratic (0 : ResidueField A) 1 0 =
      (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) (ResidueField A)) * MvPowerSeries.X 1 from by
        simp [nodalBinaryQuadratic]]
    exact ⟨eK⟩
  have key : IsNodalAlgebra k A ↔
      Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k (ResidueField A) ∧ HasNodalCompletion k A :=
    (isNodalAlgebra_tfae k A).out 1 3
  have hA : IsNodalAlgebra k A := key.mpr ⟨hsep, hNC⟩
  -- nodality, from clause (2) of the equivalences of Stacks 0C4D
  have hnode : IsNode k X x := ((isNode_tfae_of_isClosed k X hdim x hx).out 2 1).mp hA
  have hbr : numberOfBranchesOfLocalRing A = 2 :=
    (nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X_iff_numberOfBranches_eq_two k A hA).mp
      ⟨eK⟩
  exact ⟨hnode, hbij,
    (nonempty_quadraticAlgebra_algEquiv_prod_iff_numberOfBranches_eq_two k A hA).mpr hbr⟩

/-- **At a closed point of a one-dimensional scheme locally of finite type over `k`, being a
split node is exactly having completed local ring `k[[x, y]]/(x y)` as a `k`-algebra.**

This is the equivalence (1) ⟺ (3) of Stacks Tag 0CBW; the tag itself, which also carries the
description (2) of the fibre of the normalization, is
`Stacks.Curves.isSplitNode_tfae_normalizationFibre_adicCompletion`. -/
public theorem isSplitNode_iff_nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 1) (x : X) (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X)) :
    letI : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
        X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    (IsSplitNode k X x ↔
      Nonempty (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) (X.presheaf.stalk x) ≃ₐ[k]
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸
          Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) *
            MvPowerSeries.X 1}))) :=
  ⟨nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X_of_isSplitNode k X hdim x,
    isSplitNode_of_nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X k X hdim x hx⟩

/-- **Stacks 0CBW.** Let `k` be a field, let `X` be a one-dimensional algebraic `k`-scheme and
let `x ∈ X` be a closed point. The following are equivalent:

1. `x` is a split node;
2. `x` is a node and there are exactly two points `x₁, x₂` of the normalization `X^ν` lying over
   `x`, with `k = κ(x₁) = κ(x₂)`;
3. `𝒪^∧_{X,x} ≅ k[[x, y]]/(x y)` as a `k`-algebra.

Clause (4) of the source is the placeholder "add more here" and carries no mathematical content,
so the equivalence stated here is that of clauses (1), (2) and (3).

The two points of clause (2) are the branches of `𝒪_{X,x}`, counted by the fibre of the
normalization (Stacks Tag 0C1S) and by the splitting of the quadratic algebra (Stacks Tag 0CBU);
their residue fields are computed in
`Stacks.Curves.bijective_fieldToResidue_normalization_of_isNodalAlgebra`. -/
@[stacks 0CBW]
public theorem isSplitNode_tfae_normalizationFibre_adicCompletion
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim X = 1) (x : X) (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set X)) :
    letI : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
        X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
    let ν := normalizationOverField k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))
    let c₁ : Prop := IsSplitNode k X x
    let c₂ : Prop :=
      IsNode k X x ∧
        ∃ x₁ x₂ : normalizationSchemeOverField k (X ↘ Spec (.of k)),
          x₁ ≠ x₂ ∧
            {y : normalizationSchemeOverField k (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) | ν y = x} = {x₁, x₂} ∧
              Function.Bijective (fieldToResidue (ν ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k))) x₁).hom ∧
                Function.Bijective (fieldToResidue (ν ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k))) x₂).hom
    let c₃ : Prop :=
      Nonempty (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) (X.presheaf.stalk x) ≃ₐ[k]
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸
          Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1}))
    List.TFAE [c₁, c₂, c₃] := by
  intro ν c₁ c₂ c₃
  let instA : Algebra k (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
      X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom.toAlgebra
  let instK : Algebra k (X.residueField x) :=
    ((X.residue x).hom.comp ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫
      (X ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫ X.presheaf.germ ⊤ x trivial).hom).toAlgebra
  let hLN : IsLocallyNoetherian X :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (X ↘ Spec (.of k))
  let A := X.presheaf.stalk x
  -- at a node, two points of the normalization above `x` is the splitting of the quadratic
  -- algebra: both say that `x` has two branches
  have hfibre : ∀ _ : IsNodalAlgebra k A,
      Set.encard {y : normalizationSchemeOverField k (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) | ν y = x} = 2 ↔
        Nonempty (quadraticAlgebra A ≃ₐ[ResidueField A] (ResidueField A × ResidueField A)) := by
    intro hA
    rw [← numberOfBranches_eq_encard_normalizationFiber X
      (finite_irreducibleComponents_of_locallyOfFiniteType k (X ↘ Spec (.of k))) x]
    exact (nonempty_quadraticAlgebra_algEquiv_prod_iff_numberOfBranches_eq_two k A hA).symm
  tfae_have 1 → 2 := by
    intro hsplit
    have hA : IsNodalAlgebra k A := isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isSplitNode k X hdim x hsplit
    obtain ⟨x₁, x₂, hne, hset⟩ := Set.encard_eq_two.mp ((hfibre hA).mpr hsplit.2.2)
    have hres : ∀ z ∈ ({x₁, x₂} : Set _),
        Function.Bijective (fieldToResidue (ν ≫ (X ↘ Spec (.of k))) z).hom := fun z hz ↦
      bijective_fieldToResidue_normalization_of_isNodalAlgebra k (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) x hA
        hsplit.2.1 hsplit.2.2 z (hset.ge hz)
    exact ⟨hsplit.1, x₁, x₂, hne, hset, hres x₁ (Set.mem_insert _ _),
      hres x₂ (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ rfl)⟩
  tfae_have 2 → 1 := by
    rintro ⟨hnode, x₁, x₂, hne, hset, hres₁, -⟩
    have h₁ : ν x₁ = x := hset.ge (Set.mem_insert _ _)
    have hresx : Function.Bijective (fieldToResidue (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) x).hom :=
      bijective_fieldToResidue_of_bijective_fieldToResidue_normalization k
        (X ↘ Spec (.of k)) x x₁ h₁ hres₁
    have hA : IsNodalAlgebra k A :=
      isNodalAlgebra_stalk_of_isNode_of_bijective k X hdim x hnode hresx
    exact ⟨hnode, hresx,
      (hfibre hA).mp (Set.encard_eq_two.mpr ⟨x₁, x₂, hne, hset⟩)⟩
  tfae_have 1 → 3 :=
    nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X_of_isSplitNode k X hdim x
  tfae_have 3 → 1 :=
    isSplitNode_of_nonempty_algEquiv_adicCompletion_quotient_X_mul_X k X hdim x hx
  tfae_finish

